For a double-slit experiment, the fringe spacing is

\[
\Delta y = \frac{\lambda L}{d}
\]

Using yellow light with \(\lambda \approx 600 \text{ nm} = 6\times10^{-7}\text{ m}\), \(L=1\text{ m}\), and \(d=0.1\text{ mm}=1\times10^{-4}\text{ m}\):

\[
\Delta y = \frac{(6\times10^{-7})(1)}{1\times10^{-4}}
= 6\times10^{-3}\text{ m}
= 6\text{ mm}
\]

The answer is (I)<｜hy_end:6124c78e｜>
